d":"u-o","title":"cup / cop","tip":"u in cup is short, in the middle of the mouth. o in cop (American) is open and low, like a short “ah”.","pairs":[["cup","cop"],["cut","cot"],["luck","lock"],["duck","dock"],["nut","not"],["hut","hot"],["rub","rob"],["shut","shot"],["dull","doll"],["color","collar"],["bucks","box"],["stuck","stock"],["fund","fond"],["rubber","robber"]]},{"id":"er-ar","title":"heard / hard","tip":"For er in heard your mouth stays almost closed and your tongue curls from the start. ar in hard starts with an open “ah”, then the r.","pairs":[["heard","hard"],["burn","barn"],["firm","farm"],["hurt","heart"],["fur","far"],["stir","star"],["perk","park"],["curve","carve"],["dirt","dart"]]},{"id":"n-ng","title":"sin / sing","tip":"n: the tip of your tongue touches the roof of your mouth behind your teeth. ng is made at the back of your mouth, with no g sound at the end: sing, not “sing-g”.","pairs":[["sin","sing"],["thin","thing"],["win","wing"],["ran","rang"],["sun","sung"],["ban","bang"],["kin","king"],["ton","tongue"],["run","rung"]]},{"id":"th-s","title":"think / sink","tip":"th in think: the tip of your tongue goes between your teeth. s in sink: your tongue stays inside.","pairs":[["think","sink"],["thick","sick"],["thank","sank"],["mouth","mouse"],["path","pass"],["theme","seem"],["faith","face"],["thumb","sum"],["thought","sought"],["myth","miss"],["tenth","tense"]]},{"id":"ch-sh","title":"chair / share","tip":"ch starts with a short stop, like “t” + “sh”. sh is one long sound with no stop.","pairs":[["chair","share"],["chip","ship"],["cheap","sheep"],["watch","wash"],["catch","cash"],["match","mash"],["chop","shop"],["cheat","sheet"],["chin","shin"],["choose","shoes"],["witch","wish"],["chew","shoe"],["ditch","dish"]]},{"id":"u-oo","title":"full / fool","tip":"u in full is short and relaxed, with loose lips. oo in fool is long, with tight round lips.","pairs":[["full","fool"],["pull","pool"],["foot","food"],["took","tool"],["cook","cool"],["book","boot"],["stood","stool"],["look","loop"]]},{"id":"r-l","title":"right / light","tip":"For r the tip of your tongue curls back and touches nothing. For l the tip of your tongue touches the roof right behind your top teeth.","pairs":[["right","light"],["road","load"],["rock","lock"],["race","lace"],["pray","play"],["grass","glass"],["fry","fly"],["crowd","cloud"],["wrong","long"],["rate","late"],["rain","lane"],["rip","lip"],["reef","leaf"],["free","flee"],["correct","collect"],["berry","belly"]]},{"id":"w-v","title":"west / vest","tip":"For w your lips make a small round circle and the teeth don't touch anything. For v your top teeth touch your lower lip.","pairs":[["west","vest"],["wine","vine"],["went","vent"],["worse","verse"],["while","vile"],["wow","vow"],["wet","vet"],["wary","very"],["wan","van"]]},{"id":"th-d","title":"they / day","tip":"th in they: the tip of your tongue is between your teeth and your throat buzzes. d in day: the tongue taps the roof behind your teeth.","pairs":[["they","day"],["then","den"],["there","dare"],["though","dough"],["breathe","breed"],["thy","die"],["loathe","load"],["wither","wider"]]},{"id":"th-t","title":"thin / tin","tip":"th in thin: the tip of your tongue is between your teeth and air flows out. t in tin: a quick tap and a small puff.","pairs":[["thin","tin"],["three","tree"],["thank","tank"],["thought","taught"],["bath","bat"],["math","mat"],["path","pat"],["theme","team"],["thigh","tie"]]},{"id":"j-ch","title":"jeep / cheap","tip":"j in jeep is voiced: your throat buzzes. ch in cheap has no buzz, with a puff of air.","pairs":[["jeep","cheap"],["gin","chin"],["jest","chest"],["joke","choke"],["jar","char"],["badge","batch"],["ridge","rich"],["junk","chunk"]]},{"id":"o-a","title":"hot / hat","tip":"o in hot (American) is open “ah”, with the mouth wide and the tongue low and back. a in hat is a bright sound, your jaw drops and the tongue is forward.","pairs":[["hot","hat"],["lock","lack"],["cop","cap"],["pot","pat"],["rock",